## PHASE 1 — CONFIRMED BUGS TO FIX (found by code audit)

### 1.1 Routing is broken (this is why clicking a prompt image/card feels dead or glitchy)
- `openPromptDetail()` sets `location.hash = '#prompt/<id>'`, then calls `navigateTo('details')`.
- `navigateTo()` sees the hash is not `#details` and **overwrites it with `#details`**.
- Both hash changes fire `hashchange` → `handleHashRouting()` → `openPromptDetail(id,false)` runs again. Result: the view counter increments twice, the URL ends as `#details` (which `handleHashRouting` does not handle), refresh/back/share links break, and the page can flash or appear unresponsive.
- `handleHashRouting()` also ignores `#details`, `#dashboard`, `#blog/<slug>`.

**Fix:** Replace with one small router module (`src/router.ts`):
- Use the **History API with real paths** (`/`, `/search?q=`, `/prompt/:id`, `/collections`, `/blog`, `/blog/:slug`, `/about`, `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/cookies`, `/contact`, `/docs`, `/dashboard`) with `pushState` + `popstate`. `firebase.json` already has the SPA rewrite.
- `navigateTo(view, { push = true })` must never trigger itself recursively. Use a re-entrancy guard.
- Increment prompt views **once per page visit per prompt** (guard with a `Set` in `sessionStorage`).
- Back/forward, refresh, deep links and "share" links must all work. Update canonical/og tags and `document.title` per route.
- Unknown routes → a proper 404 view. Unauthenticated access to `/dashboard` → open login modal, then return.

### 1.2 Cards: whole card + image must be reliably clickable
- Replace all inline `onclick="openPromptDetail('${p.id}')"` with **one delegated click listener** using `data-prompt-id`. Same for copy, bookmark, like buttons (stopPropagation handled in the delegate).
- Make each card keyboard-accessible (`role="link"`, `tabindex="0"`, Enter/Space) and render a real `<a href="/prompt/ID">` so it works with middle-click, SEO crawlers and long-press on mobile.
- Image layers: the blurred background `<img>` must have `pointer-events-none` and `aria-hidden`; the main image must have `draggable="false"`. Do not start images at `opacity-0` waiting for `onload` (cached images and failed loads stay invisible → blank dark box). Use a skeleton background + `loading="lazy"` + `decoding="async"` + explicit `width/height` or aspect ratio, and a **visible placeholder on error** instead of hiding the image.
- Same fix for the trending cards (`app.ts` ~L1066), search autocomplete results (~L2649), related/recommended grids and sidebar widgets.

### 1.3 `handleSavePromptForm` does not exist
`index.html` has `<form id="prompt-crud-form" onsubmit="handleSavePromptForm(event)">` but no such function exists anywhere in `src/app.ts` or on `window`. Submitting the user "Submit Prompt / Edit Prompt" form throws a ReferenceError and the form can reload the page. `openUserSubmitModal`, `editUserPrompt`, `deleteUserPromptConfirm` already exist but cannot save.
**Implement** `handleSavePromptForm` (via `addEventListener('submit')`, no inline handler):
- Validate: title 5–120 chars, prompt 10–5000, negative ≤1000, tool/category must exist in the loaded lists, tags ≤10 each ≤30 chars, image URL must be https and from Cloudinary/Unsplash, or upload a file through `uploadToCloudinary`.
- Create: `status: 'pending'`, `creatorId = auth.uid`, `creator = displayName`, `views/likes/downloads/copyCount = 0`, `featured: false`, `trending: false`, `createdAt/updatedAt = serverTimestamp()`.
- Edit: only the owner, only while `pending`/`draft`; never allow changing `status`, `featured`, `trending`, counters, `creatorId`.
- Disable the submit button + show spinner while saving, show clear success/error toast, close modal, refresh "My submissions".

### 1.4 DOM ids referenced in code but missing from `index.html`
`ai-assistant-modal, ai-assist-idea, ai-assist-tool, ai-assist-style, ai-assist-output-text, explore-tools-grid, hero-left-panel, hero-right-panel, live-ai-trends-ticker, stats-counter-bar, pf-tool`, plus legacy `admin-panel-*` / `admin-*` ids that belong to the old in-page admin. These features silently do nothing. For each: either add the missing markup (if the feature is wanted: AI Prompt Builder modal, hero side panels, trends ticker, explore-tools grid) or delete the dead code. Add a dev-time helper that warns in the console when a `getElementById` returns null for a required element.
Also: `closeSeasonalComposer` is used in `admin.ts` inline onclick but is not exposed on `window` → expose it or (better) remove inline handlers in the admin (see 3.3).

### 1.5 Missing Firestore composite indexes → wrong/empty gallery
`firestore.indexes.json` is empty, but `loadInitialPrompts()` runs queries like
`where(status=='approved') + orderBy(createdAt|likes|views)` and `where(status) + where(trending) + orderBy(likes)`. These fail without indexes, so the code silently falls back to an **unordered** query and the home page order/trending/"load more" are wrong. Audit **every** `query(...)` in `app.ts`, `admin.ts`, `ads.ts` and generate the complete `firestore.indexes.json`. Also make the fallback log a clear warning instead of hiding the problem.

### 1.6 Site can fail to load because of unguarded Analytics
`firebase.ts`: `getAnalytics(app)` is called unconditionally. It throws in browsers where Analytics is unsupported or blocked (ad-blockers, private mode, some in-app browsers) and can break the whole module graph. Use `isSupported().then(...)` lazily, wrapped in try/catch, and only after cookie consent.

### 1.7 Real-time listener churn on the home page
The home gallery uses `onSnapshot` on a query ordered by `views/likes`. Every view/like/copy increment by any visitor re-fires the snapshot and re-renders the whole grid (flicker, jumping cards, high Firestore read cost, wrong "Load more" cursor). Use `getDocs` for the gallery and trending sections (refresh on demand or every few minutes), keep `onSnapshot` only for small config collections and the current user's bookmarks/likes. `renderAll()` on every auth change should only re-render the parts that depend on auth.

### 1.8 Misc functional issues
- `navigateTo` writes `#dashboard`, `#details` etc. into the hash; `view-dashboard` is not routed (fixed by 1.1).
- Hero "cursor glow" mousemove handler runs on touch devices and adds cost: attach only if `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` and not `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- `lucide.createIcons()` is called after nearly every render (dozens of full-document scans). Switch to the npm package with explicit icon imports (tree-shaken) and a single debounced `refreshIcons()` helper scoped to the changed container.
- Branding is inconsistent (PromptVerse / PromptsVerse / PromptsOne; domain `promptsone.com`, Firebase project `promptsverse-ai`). Pick one name from `siteConfigs` and use it everywhere (titles, toasts, auth modal, footer, schema.org, sitemap).
- Seeding: confirm no client code writes seed data to Firestore for normal visitors; if any seeding exists, it must be admin-only and idempotent.
- `loadMorePrompts` must use the same sort/filter/cursor as the initial query, de-duplicate by id, and hide the button when finished.

