## PHASE 3 — SECURITY HARDENING

### 3.1 Rewrite `firestore.rules` (current rules have real holes)
Problems in the current file — fix all:
1. `prompts`: `allow read: if true` exposes **pending/rejected** prompts to everyone. → read allowed only if `resource.data.status == 'approved'` OR owner OR admin.
2. `prompts` `allow create: if isSignedIn()` has **no validation**: any user can create a prompt with `status:'approved'`, `featured:true`, fake `creatorId`, huge counters. → On create require: `creatorId == request.auth.uid`, `status == 'pending'`, `featured == false`, `trending == false`, counters all `0`, key whitelist (`keys().hasOnly([...])`), string types and max sizes (title ≤120, prompt ≤5000, negative ≤1000, tags list ≤10), `request.auth.token.email_verified == true`.
3. `prompts` update: the owner can currently edit their own pending prompt **including setting `status:'approved'`**, and **any signed-in user can set counters to any value** (`hasOnly(['views','likes','downloads','copyCount'])` with no value check). → Owner update: forbid changing `status, featured, trending, creatorId, views, likes, downloads, copyCount, createdAt`. Counter update by non-owner/non-admin: only one key at a time and **exactly +1** (`request.resource.data.views == resource.data.views + 1`) on approved prompts. Likes must be tied to the per-user `users/{uid}/likes/{promptId}` doc created in the same batch (use `getAfter`/`existsAfter`).
4. `users`: `allow read: if isSignedIn()` lets any logged-in user read **every user's email and profile**. → read only owner or admin. Create: `isOwner && role=='user'` and `email == request.auth.token.email`. Update: owner may change only `displayName, photoURL, updatedAt`.
5. `siteConfigs/stats`: the extra `allow update` has **no auth requirement** → anonymous users can write `copiedToday` to any value (even a string). → require `isSignedIn()` (or App Check) and `copiedToday == resource.data.copiedToday + 1`, number type.
6. `adEvents` and `contactSubmissions` `create: if true` → unlimited spam/cost. → validate keys, types, max lengths, `timestamp == request.time`; contact messages ≤2000 chars; add App Check enforcement; keep reads admin-only.
7. `searchLogs`, `mediaLibrary`: validate fields and sizes the same way.
8. Make `isAdmin()` check the custom claim first (`request.auth.token.admin == true`) and fall back to the `users` doc to save reads.
9. Keep the default-deny catch-all. Add a `rules_test` folder with `@firebase/rules-unit-testing` + Firestore emulator tests covering: anonymous read approved vs pending, user create valid/invalid prompt, user self-promote attempt, counter +1 vs +1000, admin CRUD, users listing denied.

### 3.2 XSS — currently the biggest app-level risk
Nearly every `innerHTML` in `app.ts` interpolates database/user content **unescaped**: `p.title, p.prompt, p.creator, p.category, p.tool, photoURL, blog title/body, featuredImage, site headline (innerHTML = data.headline), toast messages, option values`. A user-submitted prompt title like `"><img src=x onerror=...>` runs JavaScript in every visitor's (and the admin's) session.
**Fix:**
- Create `src/utils/dom.ts` with `escapeHtml()`, `escapeAttr()`, `safeUrl()` (allow only `https:`, plus `data:image/` where needed; reject `javascript:`), and a tiny `html` tagged-template helper that escapes interpolations by default.
- Apply it to **every** template string in `app.ts`, `admin.ts`, `ads.ts` (admin.ts already has an `escapeHtml` at the bottom but uses it in only two places — apply everywhere and move it to the shared util).
- Blog posts / static pages / FAQ that legitimately contain HTML: sanitize with **DOMPurify** (strict allow-list) before `innerHTML`.
- Use `textContent` for all plain text sets (toast, titles, counts).
- `injectThirdPartyScripts()` currently builds `<script>` elements with `innerHTML` from admin-configured settings. Change it to accept **only IDs** validated by regex (GA4 `G-XXXX`, Clarity id, Pixel id) and generate the snippet in code. Never inject raw admin-pasted script.
- Remove all inline `onclick=` / `onsubmit=` in `index.html`, `admin.html`, and template strings; use delegated listeners with `data-action` attributes. This allows a strict CSP without `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts.

### 3.3 Hosting security headers (`firebase.json`)
Add for `**`: `Content-Security-Policy` (default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' + exact Google/AdSense/Analytics/Firebase hosts you actually use; img-src 'self' data: https://res.cloudinary.com https://images.unsplash.com + ad hosts; connect-src for firestore/identitytoolkit/securetoken/googleapis/cloudinary; frame-src for AdSense and `https://promptsverse-ai.firebaseapp.com` auth iframe; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'), `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`, `Permissions-Policy` (camera/mic/geolocation off), `Strict-Transport-Security` (1 year, includeSubDomains), and `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups` (required so Google sign-in popup keeps working). For `/admin` and `/admin.html`: `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `Cache-Control: no-store`.
Cache: `/assets/**` → `public, max-age=31536000, immutable`; `index.html` and `admin.html` → `no-cache`.
Test that Google sign-in, AdSense, Analytics, Cloudinary images and Firestore still work with the CSP (use report-only first, then enforce).

### 3.4 Secrets, keys and repo hygiene
- `.env.example` currently contains **real** values (Firebase API key, Cloudinary cloud/preset). Replace with placeholders. Firebase web API keys are public by design, but the key must be **restricted** (owner step) and `firebase.ts` should read config from `import.meta.env.VITE_FIREBASE_*` with a build-time check that fails if any are missing.
- `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `@google/genai` are in the project but unused in the client. Remove from client deps. If AI features are wanted, call Gemini only from a **Firebase Cloud Function** (callable, App Check + auth required, per-user rate limit). Never put it in `import.meta.env` / `define`.
- Delete from the repo/zip: `.aistudio/` folder, duplicate PNG in `public/assets/aistudio/`, empty `bun.lock`, `src/main.tsx`, `src/App.tsx`, `src/vite-env` leftovers not needed, duplicate `google93e1f106c7169015.html` in project root (keep only the one in `public/`).
- Cloudinary: client-side type/size checks are bypassable. Document the owner steps to lock the unsigned preset (allowed formats, max file size, fixed folder, no overwrite, no `resource_type` raw, moderation) or migrate to **signed uploads** via a Cloud Function. Also `uploadToCloudinary` forces `w_800` in the stored URL, which permanently degrades large images: store the original secure_url and apply transformations only at render time with `optimizeCloudinaryUrl(url, width)` (card 480, detail 1200).
- Enable **Firebase App Check** (reCAPTCHA Enterprise/v3) in the client and enforce for Firestore.

### 3.5 Other
- Rate-limit client-side actions that write (copy, like, view) with debounce and per-session guards.
- `robots.txt`: keep `/admin` disallowed but remember it advertises the path; `admin.html` already has `noindex`. Add `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` header for admin.
